   "name": "gap_abduce_endpoints",
   "comment": "ABDUCE THE GENERATOR FROM THE GAP'S TWO ENDPOINTS. Flag ON (agent.gap_abduce_enabled==1). On a gap-sequence Observation (status=='gap_seq'), solve G^(gap+1)(f_before) = f_after for G and write the verdict. The DECISION is this rule's; the Term supplies the arithmetic. 'abduced' is the admissibility verdict (a divisibility test, NO THRESHOLD); 'closes' is the independently-computed check that G^steps actually REACHES f_after (construction-true on the translate branch, and computed rather than asserted because a check that is never evaluated is an inert instrument); 'abduce_correction' is the symmetric-difference cell count at the far bank -- 0 iff it closes, the quantity BlinkBridge reported as 32 at this same topology. 'abduce_reason' separates the refusals by KIND (identity / indivisible / not_rigid / no_gap_structure) so a null is DIAGNOSABLE rather than a shrug. status flips to 'gap_abduced'.",
